{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghnjbx6cNXCWXVdmsGmU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fit gives Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 618 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 2490 cm⁻¹. The spin-allowed bands fix Dq and B. The spin-forbidden band then fixes C.\n\n**Dq.** For a d³ octahedral complex, ν₁ = ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₂g = 10Dq. So 10Dq = 17 500 cm⁻¹ and Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B.** The sum of the two upper spin-allowed bands is ν₂ + ν₃ = 15B + 3·(10Dq).\n- 23 860 + 37 910 = 61 770 cm⁻¹, and 3·(10Dq) = 52 500 cm⁻¹.\n- So 15B = 9270 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 618 cm⁻¹.\n\nI checked this against the splitting ν₃ − ν₂ = √(225B² + Δ² − 18BΔ), with Δ = 10Dq. The formula gives about 14 054 cm⁻¹, against 14 050 cm⁻¹ observed, so B is consistent.\n\n**C.** The lowest spin-forbidden band is ²Eg(G) ← ⁴A₂g, observed at 12 090 cm⁻¹. I computed the full d³ term energies at Dq = 1750 and B = 618 cm⁻¹.\n- At C = 2800 cm⁻¹, ²Eg falls at 13 021 cm⁻¹. That is too high, and the slope is about 3 per unit of C.\n- At C = 2490 cm⁻¹, ²Eg falls at 12 077 cm⁻¹, within about 13 cm⁻¹ of the observed band.\n- The same calculation puts ⁴T₂g at 17 500, ⁴T₁g(a) at 23 858 and ⁴T₁g(b) at 37 912 cm⁻¹, which match the three observed bands.\n\nThis gives C/B ≈ 4.0.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1750, \"B\": 618, \"C\": 2490, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from ν1/10, B from ν2+ν3−3ν1, C fitted to the 2Eg spin-forbidden band at 12090 cm-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2214,"cache_read_input_tokens":10769,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2214,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":790,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f62414a-a6ff-424d-9b29-a2b19eb4d518","uuid":"b299c63f-c7e4-4235-bd5d-c0fea09ef402","timestamp":"20